  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/zen-browser/desktop/tarball/1.24.2b",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/zen-browser/desktop/zipball/1.24.2b",
  "body": "# Zen Stable Release\r\n\r\n\r\n## Security\r\n- https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/security/advisories/mfsa2026-125/\r\n\r\n## New Features\r\n- Updated to Firefox 160.0\r\n- Added pause context menu button for the downloads section\r\n- The urlbar now has a bit of transparency for a more modern look.\r\n- The Picture-in-Picture player now has a playback speed setting, with options ranging from 0.25x to 2.0x speed. The setting appears only when the player window is medium-sized or larger.\r\n- Pages saved as PDF now make mathematical content (MathML) accessible to assistive technology such as screen readers.\r\n- Websites that repeatedly ask to handle email (mailto:) and other links can now be blocked with a new “Never allow” button, and blocked sites can be managed in Settings.\r\n- Zen now plays Matroska (MKV) files with FLAC, MP3, or PCM audio.\r\n- WebGL content on macOS is now rendered using Apple's Metal graphics API, which can improve performance on some sites.\r\n\r\n## Fixes\r\n- Improved performance for boosts color tinting.\r\n- Fixed the first character typed into the address bar or search bar sometimes being lost when typing quickly right after clicking into it.\r\n- Fixed Zen freezing for several seconds when signing in to intranet sites that use NTLM or Kerberos (Negotiate) authentication.\r\n- Fixed double-tapping or long-pressing a word to select it, and tapping to place the cursor, not working near the cursor in text fields.\r\n- Fixed links opened in the background from other apps on macOS, such as RSS readers, bringing Zen to the foreground.\r\n- Fixed downloaded files on macOS sometimes opening in the wrong application instead of the default one set in Finder.\r\n- Fixed simultaneous downloads on macOS never finishing when Zen is set to ask where to save files. Only the first file showed a save dialog.\r\n- Restored meaningful filenames and the usual save workflow for PDFs opened in Preview from the macOS print dialog.\r\n- More bug fixes and improvements.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- The address bar context menu now shows \"Paste and Search\" instead of \"Paste and Go\" when the copied text is a search term rather than a web address.\r\n",
